      "ownershipVehicle": "Meridiam Infr. S.a.r.l. (MI LBJ)",
      "description": "LBJ Infrastructure Group, LLC is the concession company and TIFIA borrower for LBJ Express, a managed-lanes toll concession in Dallas County, Texas. Under a 52-year DBFOM comprehensive development agreement with the Texas Department of Transportation through 2061, the company financed, reconstructed, operates, and maintains approximately 13.25 miles of I-635 and I-35E, including dynamically priced managed lanes alongside rebuilt general-purpose and frontage roads. The project reached financial close in June 2010, began construction in January 2011, and fully opened in September 2015. Ferrovial's SEC-filed May 2026 factbook reports Cintra at 54.60%, APG at 28.33%, and Meridiam at 17.07%; Meridiam's current portfolio page identifies the corresponding non-Cintra vehicles as LBJ Blocker and MI LBJ.",
